@* The same diagram the review page draws, fed from the classes already on disk instead of from
   the model discovery produced. Review answers "what will be written"; this answers "what is
   written". *@
@page "/relationships"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@using CodeGenerator.Web.Relationships
@inject RelationshipView View

<PageTitle>Relationships</PageTitle>

@* Interactive even though nothing on the page responds to anything, and that is the point: the
   circuit IS the mechanism. CircuitWatch.ShouldAbandon only fires once a tab has connected and
   gone, so a statically-rendered page opens no circuit, is never seen to close, and leaves the
   console holding the prompt until Ctrl-C. It also puts the PageTitle through the HeadOutlet,
   which App.razor renders interactively for the same reason. *@
@* The "chat" class is load-bearing, not decoration: every colour token in chat.css is declared on
   the .chat class rather than on :root, precisely so that one page's palette cannot repaint the
   other. Without it here, every var() on this page resolves to nothing and the diagram comes out
   unpainted. *@
<div class="chat rel-page">
    <header class="rel-head">
        <h1>Relationships</h1>
        <p class="rel-root">@View.Root</p>
    </header>

    <RelationshipDiagram Sources="View.Sources" />
</div>
